# MRG Migration Utility — Runbook

**Team:** Midrange Engineering (MRG)
**Maintained by:** OS Engineering — Midrange Engineering Team
**Last Updated:** June 2026

---

## Overview

The MRG Migration Utility is an end-to-end workflow that allows application teams to submit structured data migration and ownership transfer requests to Midrange Engineering. The request is fulfilled by a Midrange Change Team engineer running an AAP job that processes the submitted CSV against the target servers.

This runbook covers everything the Change Team engineer needs to know: what the request looks like, how to validate it, how to run it, and what the output means.

---

## How the Workflow Works

1. The application team fills out the **Migration Request Portal** (internal web tool) and downloads a CSV file
2. They attach the CSV to a **ServiceNow request** submitted to the Midrange team
3. A Midrange Change Team engineer picks up the ticket, reviews the CSV, uploads it to the jumpbox, and runs the AAP job
4. The job executes the migration script on the jumpbox and outputs a full run log
5. The engineer reviews the output, updates the ticket, and closes

---

## Step 1 — Review the ServiceNow Request

When a migration ticket comes in, check the following before touching anything:

- The ticket has a CSV file attached
- The CSV filename follows the format: `migration_request_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS.csv`
- The request description is clear about what is being migrated and why
- If anything looks off or incomplete, send it back to the requester before proceeding

> **Note:** Do not modify the CSV. If corrections are needed, the requester must re-export from the portal and resubmit.

---

## Step 2 — Understand the CSV Format

The CSV downloaded from the portal will look like this:

```
#Type,Source server,Destination server,Source path,Destination path,Source user,Target user,Source group,Target group
DATA_TRANSFER,rhel8-app01.dc1.corp,rhel9-app01.dc2.corp,/app/data/jdoe/reports,/var/app/data/reports,jdoe,CORP\ad_jdoe,appgrp,CORP\ad_appgrp
OWNERSHIP_TRANSFER,rhel8-app02.dc1.corp,,/app/data/svcacct/config,,,svcacct01,CORP\svc_acct01,svcgrp,CORP\ad_svcgrp
```

### Row Types

| Type | What it does |
|---|---|
| `DATA_TRANSFER` | Copies data from source server/path to destination server/path, optionally remapping user and group ownership |
| `OWNERSHIP_TRANSFER` | Changes ownership of files on a single server in-place — no data is moved |

### Column Reference

| Column | Description |
|---|---|
| `#Type` | `DATA_TRANSFER` or `OWNERSHIP_TRANSFER` |
| `Source server` | Hostname of the source (always required) |
| `Destination server` | Hostname of the destination (DT only, blank for OT) |
| `Source path` | Full path on the source server |
| `Destination path` | Full path on the destination server (DT only) |
| `Source user` | Existing local user to remap (optional) |
| `Target user` | AD user to remap to (optional) |
| `Source group` | Existing local group to remap (optional) |
| `Target group` | AD group to remap to (optional) |

