## Step 7 — Review the Logs on the Jumpbox

Two log files are written per run under `/data/MRGeng/Migration_Utility/logs/`:

| File | Contents |
|---|---|
| `migration_request_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS.run.log` | Full structured run log — parse results, precheck results, per-row status, summary |
| `migration_request_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS.rsync.log` | Raw rsync output for every row that executed |

```bash
cat /data/MRGeng/Migration_Utility/logs/migration_request_20260611_103701.run.log
cat /data/MRGeng/Migration_Utility/logs/migration_request_20260611_103701.rsync.log
```

---

## Step 8 — Check CSV Final Status

After a live run, the CSV is automatically moved based on outcome:

| Outcome | CSV location |
|---|---|
| All rows succeeded | `processed/migration_request_....csv` |
| Any row skipped or failed | `failed/migration_request_....csv` |
| Dry run or aborted | Stays in `pending/migration_request_....csv` |

```bash
ls -ltr /data/MRGeng/Migration_Utility/processed/
ls -ltr /data/MRGeng/Migration_Utility/failed/
```

If the CSV ended up in `failed/`, review the run log summary section for which rows failed and why, then communicate back to the requester.

